What is a "bag of words" in c++? Answer: I see you've got a project to do!  The document you're trying to classify should be encoded as a feature vector, with each element in the vector indicating the presence or absence of a word in the document.   So you might have a list of words:

std::vector<std::string> words(3);
words[0] = "Kitty";
words[1] = "Puppy";
words[2] = "Moocow";

Then represent your document as a list of bool:

std::vector<bool> wordbag(3);

If the doc contains the word "Kitty", set wordbag[0] to true.  If the doc contains the word "Moocow", set wordbag[2] to true.  Then you can decide how to classify the document based on your wordbag.

